From: "Shawn Grover" <irisinc@telusplanet.net>
Subject: VAX Connectivity to NT????
Date: 1997/12/12
Message-ID: <01bd069c$c09ef670$01c8a8c0@iris_s>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 297412868
Organization: RHA5
Newsgroups: comp.os.vms,comp.sys.vms,microsoft.public.windowsnt.misc,vmsnet.admin,vmsnet.misc,vmsnet.networks.misc,vmsnet.networks.tcp-ip.misc,vmsnet.tcp.multinet


Our new site is using a VAX system and wishes access to the NT Resources
(or at least better integration with the NT network - which we run).  My
question is how to make this happen??  We know very little about VAX, so
need some help.

The techs running the VAX network have installed the TCP/IP protocol for
VAX, but have not yet activated it (the reboot is scheduled for next week).
 There is no guarantee they have configured the protocol correctly or even
if it is installed correctly.

These techs want NT to provide DNS services as well.  We know a reasonable
amount about TCP/IP, but have limited experience with DNS - we use WINS. 
Is it possible for the VAX network to use the NT DNS??  If so, does
anything special need to be done to the DNS?  I would expect the routing
tables would need to be updated...

BTW, the VAX traffic and the NT traffic both flow over the same backbone at
present.  There may be plans in the future to separate them (which would
make life easier...), but this would not happen anytime soon.

This is somewhat of an urgent thing, so please respond by email.

Thanks (and I appologize for any cross-posts).

Shawn Grover
IRIS Systems, Inc.
Calgary, Alberta, Canada
irisinc@telusplanet.net



